.TH VELOCITTY 1 "October 2026" "velocitty 1.2.1" "Velocitty \- (not) a terminal"
.SH NAME
velocitty \- (not) a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B velocitty
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-e | \-\-
.IR command " [" arg "...]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B velocitty
is (not) a terminal for Linux, Windows, and macOS: CPU-rendered and designed
first for Omarchy. Peak supplies Wayland/X11 on Linux, Win32/ConPTY on
Windows 10 1903 or later, and AppKit/POSIX PTYs on macOS 11 or later.
It is designed to keep up with high-volume output such as
.BR cat (1)
of large files: PTY input is truncated through a mirrored circular buffer,
split into lines and runs with SIMD, then fed to a minimal-state VT emulator
and drawn to a software framebuffer.
.PP
With no
.B \-e
command, the child is
.B $SHELL
(or
.B /bin/sh
if unset) on Linux/macOS. Windows uses
.B COMSPEC
(or
.B cmd.exe
if unset). The child environment sets
.BR TERM = xterm-256color
(SSH-safe terminfo),
.BR COLORTERM = truecolor ,
.BR TERM_PROGRAM = velocitty ,
and
.BR KITTY_WINDOW_ID
to the emulator PID.
.PP
Window class and title follow
.B \-\-class
/
.B \-\-title
and may be updated by OSC 176 and OSC 0/2. Geometry, font size, and inner
padding use CSS 96 DPI times the desktop scale: Hyprland /
.B GDK_SCALE
on Linux, per-monitor DPI on Windows, and the Retina backing scale on macOS.
Metrics are reapplied on focus and resize when the scale or grid changes.
.SH PACKAGES
Linux releases include GNU and dynamically linked musl tarballs for x86_64
and aarch64. Musl builds require the target system's musl loader and native
Wayland/X11 libraries (for example, Alpine Linux). They are not static binaries.
.PP
Windows releases provide a per-user Inno Setup installer and a portable ZIP.
macOS releases provide a universal Intel/Apple Silicon app in a DMG; drag
Velocitty.app to Applications.
.PP
Windows/macOS packages are unsigned. If Windows shows SmartScreen, choose
More info, then Run anyway. On macOS, allow Velocitty in System Settings,
Privacy & Security after the first launch attempt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\- " " \fIcommand\fR " [" \fIarg\fR ...]
Execute
.I command
in the PTY instead of the shell. All following arguments are passed to
.IR command .
Must be last among options.
.TP
.BR \-\-class " " \fIname\fR
Linux WM_CLASS instance / Wayland app-id (also
.BR \-\-class= name ).
Default:
.BR velocitty .
.TP
.BR \-\-title " " \fItext\fR
Initial window title (also
.BR \-\-title= text ).
Default:
.BR Velocitty .
.TP
.BR \-\-working\-directory " " \fIdir\fR
Working directory of the child (also
.BR \-\-working\-directory= dir ).
Used by
.BR xdg-terminal-exec (1).
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy the current selection to the system clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V
Paste CLIPBOARD into the PTY (bracketed paste if DECSET 2004 is on).
.TP
.B Shift+Insert
Same as Ctrl+Shift+V.
.PP
On macOS, Command+C and Command+V also copy and paste; Command+W or
Command+Q closes the window.
.PP
Other keys are sent as VT sequences (including application-cursor keys when
the application has enabled them).
.SH MOUSE
Left-drag selects a cell stream. Double-click selects a word; triple-click
selects a line. Releasing the button copies the selection to PRIMARY
(the Linux primary selection, or a terminal-local selection on Windows/macOS).
.PP
When mouse reporting is enabled (DECSET 1000/1002/1003, SGR/urxvt/pixel
modes), Shift+drag still selects instead of reporting. Middle-click pastes
PRIMARY. Wheel events go to the application when reporting, otherwise scroll
the primary screen history or send arrow keys on the alternate screen.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Config uses a TOML subset, similar to Alacritty. Supported settings use bare
table/key names and single-line quoted strings (including basic string escapes).
Integers are nonnegative decimal values; font sizes also accept finite floats
with exponents and digit separators. Unknown keys and tables are skipped,
including array tables, multiline strings, and nested arrays or inline tables
(up to 64 levels). The parser does not fully validate TOML.
.PP
Load order (later files overlay earlier; Omarchy theme colors win on Linux
when present):
.IP 1. 3
The platform user config: Linux
.IR ~/.config/velocitty/config.toml ,
Windows
.IR %APPDATA%/velocitty/config.toml ,
or macOS
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/velocitty/config.toml" .
If set,
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/velocitty/config.toml
overrides the platform location.
.IP 2.
.I ./config.toml
in the current working directory
.IP 3.
Linux Omarchy current theme
.I colors.toml
.IP 4.
Linux Omarchy current theme
.I alacritty.toml
.PP
If
.B [font].size
is still unset, size is taken from
.IR ~/.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml ,
then 9 pt if the current Omarchy theme's
.I colors.toml
exists, otherwise 8 pt. The default family is
.BR monospace :
fontconfig
.RB ( "omarchy font current" )
on Linux, Consolas on Windows, or Menlo on macOS.
.SS Colors
Root or
.B [colors]
/
.B [colors.primary]
keys:
.BR foreground " (" fg ),
.BR background " (" bg ),
.BR cursor .
.B [normal]
and
.B [bright]
(or
.BR [colors.normal] ,
.BR [colors.bright] )
set the 16 ANSI colors. Omarchy
.I colors.toml
keys such as
.BR muted ,
.BR bright_foreground ,
and root-level ANSI names are accepted.
.SS [general]
.TP
.BR pad " / " padding
Inner window margin in CSS pixels, all sides. Default: 14. Scaled by the
output scale factor.
.PP
Legacy
.BR refreshrate " (" hz ")"
and
.B whitelist
settings are parsed for compatibility but currently have no effect.
Refresh cadence follows the Hyprland monitor refresh rate, or 60 Hz otherwise.
.SS [font]
.TP
.BR family " / " font " / " font_family
Installed family name, resolved with fontconfig on Linux, GDI on Windows,
and Core Text on macOS. Linux primary families may use fontconfig patterns.
Default:
.BR monospace .
.TP
.B fallbacks
Array of installed font family names, in priority order, after the primary
and styled faces and before built-in coverage fonts. For example:
.nf
fallbacks = ["Symbols Nerd Font Mono", "Noto Sans Symbols 2"]
.fi
Missing families and duplicate font files are skipped; names must match an
installed family (case-insensitive), not a fontconfig pattern or generic alias.
Built-in platform symbol, CJK, and emoji coverage fonts remain enabled,
including when this array is empty (the default). Color-emoji availability
depends on the installed font format. Fonts must already be installed.
Maximum: 16 names, 128 bytes per name. A later config array replaces the
previous array; an empty array clears only the user list. Reload with
SIGUSR1 or SIGUSR2, or let the config watcher detect the change.
.TP
.BR size " / " font_size
Point size. Default: Alacritty config, else 9 pt if the current Omarchy theme's
.I colors.toml
exists, else 8 pt.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
.RS
foreground = "#ebdbb2"
background = "#282828"
cursor = "#ebdbb2"

[normal]
black = "#282828"
red = "#cc241d"
# ...

[bright]
black = "#928374"
# ...

[general]
pad = 14

[font]
family = "monospace"
fallbacks = []
size = 16
.RE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate Unix config, Omarchy state, and fontconfig.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides
.IR ~/.config
for user config and the Alacritty size fallback. User config overrides apply
on all three platforms.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Overrides
.IR ~/.local/state
for Omarchy current theme paths.
.TP
.B SHELL
Linux/macOS child program when
.B \-e
is not given.
.TP
.B COMSPEC
Windows child program when
.B \-e
is not given.
.TP
.B APPDATA
Windows user-config root; USERPROFILE/AppData/Roaming is the fallback.
.TP
.B GDK_SCALE ", " QT_SCALE_FACTOR
Linux UI scale fallback when Hyprland scale is unavailable.
.TP
.B TERM ", " COLORTERM ", " TERM_PROGRAM ", " KITTY_WINDOW_ID
Set in the child. Incoming
.B KITTY_LISTEN_ON
is cleared.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGUSR1 ", " SIGUSR2
On Linux/macOS, reload colors and font from config without restarting.
On Linux this also reloads the current Omarchy theme. Config/theme/font file
changes are watched (throttled) on all platforms and trigger the same reload;
CSI 2031 is sent when the palette changes.
.TP
.B SIGWINCH
Sent to the slave foreground process group after
.B TIOCSWINSZ
on Linux/macOS resize; Windows resizes the ConPTY.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/velocitty/config.toml
Linux user configuration.
.TP
.I %APPDATA%/velocitty/config.toml
Windows user configuration.
.TP
.I "~/Library/Application Support/velocitty/config.toml"
macOS user configuration.
.PP
XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides the platform user-config root.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/omarchy/current/theme/colors.toml
.TQ
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/omarchy/current/theme/alacritty.toml
Linux Omarchy live theme (overlaid on user config).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/alacritty/alacritty.toml
Font size fallback when unset.
.SH PROTOCOL
Implements a large subset of xterm / foot control sequences: C0/C1, ESC
charsets, CSI (SGR, CUP, DECSET/DECRQM, rectangular ops, kitty keyboard,
window ops, color stack, XTSMGRAPHICS), OSC (title, colors, OSC 8 hyperlinks,
cwd, notify, alpha, selection, cursor shape, OSC 52 clipboard, OSC 176
app-id), DCS (DECRQSS, iTerm sync, XTGETTCAP, sixel), and kitty graphics
(APC G, including
.B a=q
replies for icat). File/temporary-file kitty transfers and desktop
notifications currently use the Linux implementation. On Windows/macOS,
use streamed image transfers (for example,
.BR "icat --transfer-mode=stream" ).
.PP
DECSET 2026 and iTerm DCS
.B =1s
defer presenting frames until the synchronized update ends (1s timeout).
In-band resize (2048) flushes VT replies after a grid change.
.PP
In Debug builds only, OSC 556 and CSI
.B ? 556
toggle a visual overlay (grid, wrap, LCF, cursor, dirty, region, wide, HUD).
Ignored in Release.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xterm (1),
.BR foot (1),
.BR fc-match (1),
.BR xdg-terminal-exec (1)
.SH BUGS
There is no GPU renderer, no multiplexer, and no kitty-style CTL.
